{"name":"Black Russian","hex":"#24252b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Black Russian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to Black Russia.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see Black,‎ Russian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cocktail containing vodka and a coffee-flavoured liqueur such as Kahlúa.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see Black,‎ Russian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Black_Russian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Russian","blocks":[{"text":"The Black Russian is a cocktail of vodka and coffee liqueur. It contains 50 ml vodka and 20 ml coffee liqueur, per IBA specified ingredients."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Black_Russian.jpg/330px-Black_Russian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Russian"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg/500px-Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"ht